The sum of the angle measures in a hexagon is $180(6-2) = 720$ degrees, so we have \[\angle F + \angle I + \angle G + \angle U + \angle R + \angle E = 720^\circ.\] Given that $\angle G$ is supplementary to $\angle E$ and $\angle R$ is supplementary to $\angle U$, we have: \[\angle G + \angle E = 180^\circ \text{ and } \angle R + \angle U = 180^\circ.\] With $\angle F = \angle I = \angle U$, we can simplify the equation to:
\begin{align*}
\angle F + \angle I + \angle G + \angle U + \angle R + \angle E &= (\angle F + \angle I + \angle U) + (\angle G + \angle E) + (\angle R + \angle U)\\
&= 3\angle U + 180^\circ + 180^\circ,
\end{align*} 
thus $3\angle U + 360^\circ = 720^\circ$. Solving for $\angle U$, we have $3\angle U = 360^\circ$, so $\angle U = \boxed{120^\circ}$.

